4.7% | [Arithmetic] E=mkt cap $23.45B; D=$1.168B (LT debt $0.958B + op leases $0.210B; vendor debt cross-check matches) |\n| **WACC** | 0.953\u00d78.66% + 0.047\u00d74.10% = **8.44% \u2192 round 8.5%** | [Arithmetic] |\n\n**3-2. Explicit forecast (base case)**\n\nAll figures in $B. Revenue growth sources: FY2026 = company guidance +8.5% midpoint [Actual]; FY2027 = analyst consensus +8.2% [Estimate, stockanalysis.com]; FY2028-30 = my assumption \u2014 fade to mid-point of company's 2021 investor-day target of 5-10% [Assumption + company target]; FY2031-35 = fade to long-run nominal GDP [Assumption]. **Above FY2027, no guided numbers exist \u2014 this is the key uncertainty of the model.**\n\n| FY | Revenue | Growth | OpMgn | OpInc | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCFF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | $3.80 | +8.5% | 19.2% | $0.730 | $0.569 | $0.129 | $0.099 | $0.000 | **$0.599** |\n| 2027E | $4.11 | +8.2% | 19.5% | $0.801 | $0.625 | $0.136 | $0.107 | $0.031 | **$0.623** |\n| 2028E | $4.40 | +7.0% | 19.8% | $0.871 | $0.679 | $0.141 | $0.114 | $0.043 | **$0.663** |\n| 2029E | $4.66 | +6.0% | 20.0% | $0.932 | $0.727 | $0.144 | $0.121 | $0.040 | **$0.710** |\n| 2030E | $4.89 | +5.0% | 20.0% | $0.978 | $0.763 | $0.147 | $0.127 | $0.034 | **$0.749** |\n| 2031E | $5.09 | +4.0% | 20.0% | $1.018 | $0.794 | $0.153 | $0.132 | $0.030 | **$0.785** |\n| 2032E | $5.27 | +3.5% | 20.0% | $1.054 | $0.822 | $0.158 | $0.137 | $0.027 | **$0.816** |\n| 2033E | $5.43 | +3.0% | 20.0% | $1.086 | $0.847 | $0.163 | $0.141 | $0.024 | **$0.845** |\n| 2034E | $5.59 | +3.0% | 20.0% | $1.118 | $0.872 | $0.168 | $0.145 | $0.024 | **$0.871** |\n| 2035E | $5.73 | +2.5% | 20.0% | $1.146 | $0.894 | $0.172 | $0.143 | $0.021 | **$0.902** |\n\nAssumptions behind each driver:\n- **Revenue growth:** FY26 guided [Actual]; FY27 analyst consensus [Estimate]; FY28-30 = 7\u21925% [Assumption]; FY31-35 = 4\u21922.5% [Assumption]. Company references \">5% organic revenue CAGR\" for 2027+ in