uation-driven, not earnings-driven |\n\n**1.5-2. Deviation check**\n\nMy base-case IV ($310) implies the price deviates ~105% above fair value. This conclusion is 2\u00d7 away from base rates. Justifications:\n1. **Valuation excess is visible in the multiples:** 41.6\u00d7 forward EPS against 8\u201312% EPS growth produces a PEG >3.0; history says such gaps compress.\n2. **Growth re-acceleration is unproven:** 10-year revenue CAGR was only 4.4%; the 5-year 7.9% is a recent acceleration \u2014 extrapolating 8-9% for a decade assumes a structural shift not yet in the financial record.\n3. **The market is pricing defense as \"compound tech\" (TDG/HEICO multiples) without CW's growth rate:** HEICO/TDG trade at 40-50x with 15-20% organic growth. CW grows 8-9%. The multiple exceeds the growth-adjusted comp base.\n\n**1.5-3. Base rate shock check**\n\nMarket-implied growth of ~10% for 10 years exceeds the 15-20% base rate by ~0.5-0.7\u00d7 \u2014 not a 2\u00d7 red flag, but this is a strong upward deviation. Additional evidence required (and not available): explicit management multi-year financial targets beyond \">5% organic\" and long-term margin guidance. **Deviation is only partially justified \u2014 I keep my valuation anchored to the lower-growth path.**\n\n```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u