urrently supported by margin expansion + buybacks + defense tailwind, but the valuation already assumes it.\n\n**2-4. Financial strength scorecard (FY2025 unless noted)**\n\n| Metric | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth (5-yr CAGR) | +7.9% | [Arithmetic] |\n| TTM revenue growth | +8.0% (Q2-26 YoY +5.4%) | [Arithmetic] |\n| Revenue growth FY2026 guidance | +8\u20139% | [Actual] |\n| Operating margin (FY2025 / 12-yr median) | 18.1% / 15.4% | [Arithmetic] |\n| EPS growth (FY2025 vs FY2024) | +19.5% (12.86 \u2192 wait, NI-based: 0.484/0.405 = +19.5%) | [Arithmetic] |\n| ROE | 19.7% | [Aggregator] |\n| ROIC (approx: NOPAT 22% tax / (equity+net debt)) | ~15.4% | [Estimate] |\n| FCF margin / FCF conversion | 15.8% / 114% of NI | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net debt/EBITDA | (0.958 LT+current + 0.210 leases \u2212 0.371 cash) / 0.759 = **1.05\u00d7** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Interest coverage | 0.634 / ~0.048 \u2248 13\u00d7 | [Estimate] |\n| Net cash vs net debt | Net debt ~$0.80B | [Estimate] |\n\n**Judgment: Excellent.** F-score 8/9, accruals ratio \u22120.03 (high earnings quality), clean balance sheet, FCF conversion >110%.\n\n**2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0-15)**\n\n| Criterion | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 3/3 | Net share count \u22121.9% (1-yr), \u22122.4% (3-yr); buybacks consistently funded from FCF. Expansion to $260M buyback in 2026 \u2014 but note that repurchases at 41\u00d7 earnings are value-destructive on my numbers. |\n| M&A track record | 2/3 | Disciplined small tuck-ins; no major impairments in pack data; no large transformative M&A evidence |\n| Capex efficiency | 2/3 | Capex only 2.6% of revenue; incremental ROIC is high (>20%) given revenue growth on lean capex |\n| Rationality of mix | 3/3 | Balanced: organic capex + R&D + buybacks + modest dividend (0.15% yield) |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3/3 | Raised FY2026 guidance for sales/OI/margin/EPS/FCF in Q2; beats consistently (Q2-26 EPS beat) |\n| **Total** | **13/15** | Insider ownership 0.37% \u2014 no bonus/penalty |\n\n```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```\n\n**2.5-1. R&D capitalization.** CW does not break out R&D in the pack. Engineering/development costs run within SG&A/AOI. Estimated development spend ~2-3% of revenue (~$80-105M FY2025). Capitalizing would lift adjusted OI by ~$50-70M and adjusted ROIC to ~16-17%. **Adjustment: minor, +0.5-1pp ROIC.**\n\n**2.5-2. SBC treatment.** FY2025 SBC $22M [Actual] = 0.6% of revenue. Small. My FCFF model uses EBIT (which already expenses SBC) and does not add it back \u2014 effectively treating it as a cash expense. **Adjusted FCF after SBC \u2248 $0.55B [Estimate].**\n\n**2.5-3. Operating lease capitalization.** Op leases $210M (FY2025) [Actual]. Adjusted net debt = $958M (LT+current) + $210M \u2212 $371M cash = **$0.80B**. Coverage remains 13\u00d7; leverage still modest. **Vendor total debt $1.168B equals my LT + current + op leases sum \u2014 cross-check confirms both approach.**\n\n**2.5-4. Brand/data.** Not material for an industrial/defense company; brand value in government procurement is predominantly qualification-based. **No adjustment.**\n\n**2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC.** GAAP ROIC ~15.4%; adjusted for R&D capitalization ~16.5% [Estimate]. Gap <5pp, not material.\n\n**2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett style).**\n\n```\nOwner Earnings = Net income + D&A \u2212 Maintenance capex \u2212 \u0394WC\n= $0.484B + $0.125B \u2212 $0.060B \u2212 (\u2212$0.141B) = $0.690B   [Estimate]\n```\n\nMaintenance capex assumed ~2/3 of total capex [Assumption]. Owner earnings ~$690M \u2014 strong, 1.3\u00d7 reported NI, driven by negative working-capital requirement from customer advances on defense contracts.\n\n```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```\n\n**3-1. Discount rate derivation**\n\n| Component | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free rate (10Y UST) | 4.71% | [Actual] TradingEconomics 2026-08-21 |\n| ERP | 4.5% | [Assumption] Damodaran long-run US ERP midpoint |\n| Beta | 0.878 | [Aggregator] vendor quote (window/benchmark unstated) |\n| Cost of equity | 4.71% + 0.878 \u00d7 4.5% = **8.66%** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Pre-tax cost of debt | 5.25% | [Assumption] \u2014 credit rating not confirmed; mid-BBB/BBB+ industrial spread over 10Y |\n| After-tax cost of debt | 5.25% \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.22) = **4.10%** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Tax rate | 22% | [Assumption] \u2014 pack tax inputs broken for FY14-15; FY25 effective \u224818.5%, using 22% as conservative |\n| Weights (E / D) | 95.3% / 4.7% | [Arithmetic] E=mkt cap $23.45B; D=$1.168B (LT debt $0.958B + op leases $0.210B; vendor debt cross-check matches) |\n| **WACC** | 0.953\u00d78.66% + 0.047\u00d74.10% = **8.44% \u2192 round 8.5%** | [Arithmetic] |\n\n**3-2. Explicit forecast (base case)**\n\nAll figures in $B. Revenue growth sources: FY2026 = company guidance +8.5% midpoint [Actual]; FY2027 = analyst consensus +8.2% [Estimate, stockanalysis.com]; FY2028-30 = my assumption \u2014 fade to mid-point of company's 2021 investor-day target of 5-10% [Assumption + company target]; FY2031-35 = fade to long-run nominal GDP [Assumption]. **Above FY2027, no guided numbers exist \u2014 this is the key uncertainty of the model.**\n\n| FY | Revenue | Growth | OpMgn | OpInc | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCFF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | $3.80 | +8.5% | 19.2% | $0.730 | $0.569 | $0.129 | $0.099 | $0.000 | **$0.599** |\n| 2027E | $4.11 | +8.2% | 19.5% | $0.801 | $0.625 | $0.136 | $0.107 | $0.031 | **$0.623** |\n| 2028E | $4.40 | +7.0% | 19.8% | $0.871 | $0.679 | $0.141 | $0.114 | $0.043 | **$0.663** |\n| 2029E | $4.66 | +6.0% | 20.0% | $0.932 | $0.727 | $0.144 | $0.121 | $0.040 | **$0.710** |\n| 2030E | $4.89 | +5.0% | 20.0% | $0.978 | $0.763 | $0.147 | $0.127 | $0.034 | **$0.749** |\n| 2031E | $5.09 | +4.0% | 20.0% | $1.018 | $0.794 | $0.153 | $0.132 | $0.030 | **$0.785** |\n| 2032E | $5.27 | +3.5% | 20.0% | $1.054 | $0.822 | $0.158 | $0.137 | $0.027 | **$0.816** |\n| 2033E | $5.43 | +3.0% | 20.0% | $1.086 | $0.847 | $0.163 | $0.141 | $0.024 | **$0.845** |\n| 2034E | $5.59 | +3.0% | 20.0% | $1.118 | $0.872 | $0.168 | $0.145 | $0.024 | **$0.871** |\n| 2035E | $5.73 | +2.5% | 20.0% | $1.146 | $0.894 | $0.172 | $0.143 | $0.021 | **$0.902** |\n\nAssumptions behind each driver:\n- **Revenue growth:** FY26 guided [Actual]; FY27 analyst consensus [Estimate]; FY28-30 = 7\u21925% [Assumption]; FY31-35 = 4\u21922.5% [Assumption]. Company references \">5% organic revenue CAGR\" for 2027+ in William Blair deck (2026) [Actual, target not guidance].\n- **Op margin:** FY26 guided 19.2% [Actual]; FY27-29 expansion to 20% [Assumption \u2014 company targets OI growth > revenue growth; capping at 20% is conservative-estimate midpoint]. No managed longer-term margin target confirmed.\n- **Capex:** 2.6% of revenue \u2014 in line with FY2014-25 range (1.6-3.0%) [Arithmetic].\n- **D&A:** 3.4% fading to 3.0% of revenue [Assumption \u2014 history 3.2-5.3%, recent 3.4%].\n- **\u0394WC:** FY26 = $0 to align with company FCF guidance ($585-605M) cross-check [Actual/Assumption]; FY27+ = 10-15% of incremental revenue [Assumption \u2014 historical WC equals ~17.5% of revenue, but defense advances mitigate].\n- **Tax rate:** 22% [Assumption], conservative vs effective ~18.5% in FY25.\n\n**FY2026 cross-check:** FCFF $0.599B \u2248 guided FCF $585-605M (FCFE after ~$40M after-tax interest \u2248 $560M, within model noise). [Actual]\n\n**3-3. Terminal value & intrinsic value**\n\n| Component | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Terminal growth (g) | 2.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal GDP] |\n| Terminal FCFF (FY2036E) | $0.902 \u00d7 1.025 = $0.925B |\n| Terminal value (at end FY2035) | $0.925 / (0.085 \u2212 0.025) = **$15.42B** |\n| PV of explicit FCFF | **$5.07B** |\n| PV of terminal value | $15.42 \u00d7 0.466 = **$7.19B** |\n| Enterprise value | **$12.26B** |\n| + Cash | +$0.371B [Actual] |\n| \u2212 Debt (LT $0.958B + leases $0.210B) | \u2212$1.168B [Actual cross-checked] |\n| **Equity value** | **$11.46B** |\n| **Per share (36.93M shares)** | **$310** |\n\n**3-4. Multiples cross-check**\n\n| Multiple | Current | Fair (my thesis) | Comment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fwd P/E (FY26E EPS $15.25) | 41.6\u00d7 | 20-25\u00d7 | Quality compounder with 12% EPS growth deserves 20-24\u00d7; 41.6\u00d7 is extreme |\n| EV/EBITDA (FY26E $0.859B) | 28.2\u00d7 | 15-18\u00d7 | Historical CW range ~12-18\u00d7; current is a structural re-rating |\n| P/FCF (FY26E $595M \u2192 $16.11/sh) | 39.4\u00d7 | 20-28\u00d7 | FCF yield 2.5% \u2014 among the lowest in industrials |\n| P/B | 9.32\u00d7 | 5-7\u00d7 | Implies >8.8% perpetual growth at 10% COE; achievable only in a world where EPS grows 8%+ forever |\n| PEG (EPS growth 12.2%) | ~3.4\u00d7 (based on fwd P/E) | \u22641.5\u00d7 | Pack figure 2.0 uses a different (likely 5-yr) growth rate \u2014 [Aggregator] |\n\n**3-5. Reverse DCF (what the market price implies)**\n\nAt $635, EV = $24.25B. Solving the 10-year DCF with my terminal assumptions (g=2.5%, WACC=8.5%):\n\n- **Required FCFF CAGR (years 1-10): ~12-13%**\n- At WACC 7.5%, required FCFF CAGR: **~10%**\n\nFor reference: CW's 12-year FCFF history (proxied by FCF) grew at approximately 6-7% CAGR. The market is pricing roughly **2\u00d7 the historical growth rate**, sustained for a decade, with no margin recession.\n\n**3-6. Sensitivity \u2014 intrinsic value per share**\n\n| WACC \\ g | 2.0% | 2.5% | 3.0% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 7.5% | $391 | $420 | $456 |\n| 8.5% | $291 | **$310** | $333 |\n| 9.5% | $224 | $239 | $256 |\n\n**Range: $224 \u2013 $456.** The entire 80% CI remains below the $635 market price.\n\n```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```\n\n**3.5-1. Competitive response.** If CW keeps winning sole-source content on Virginia/Columbia, primes (HII, GD/EB) cannot easily switch suppliers mid-program \u2014 switching costs protect CW, and margins can keep expanding. Risk: primes start \"backward integrating\" into actuation/controls as their own backlog grows. Probability of a meaningful in-sourcing wave: moderate, slow-moving. Score: \u22121 (mild negative).\n\n**3.5-2. Reflexivity.** High stock price \u2192 SBC economically valuable (but CW SBC is small at 0.6% revenue); M&A currency strong; customer perception solid. Falling price \u2192 minimal risk to defense franchises given engineering-driven selection. Reflexivity is weak: CW's fundamentals are contract-driven, not market-feedback-driven. Score: 0.\n\n**3.5-3. Customer behavior evolution.** Defense demand is program-driven, not adoption-S-curve driven. As Navy submarine and AUKUS programs scale, CW moves from early-production to high-rate production \u2192 positive operating leverage, better absorption (visible in FY26 margin guidance). Commercial nuclear/SMR is early-adopter stage with 5-10 year revenue potential [Estimate]. LTV/CAC not relevant in this model.\n\n```\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25