lternative Engine 4 would require treating nuclear/SMR upside as a call option; data pack provides no segment-backed numerics for that.\n5. Alternative Engine 2 would undervalue a 10-year backlog franchise.\n\n**Model Confidence: Medium** \u2014 no segment profit data, no effective tax rate, no analyst Q&A; uncertainty explicitly carried into scenarios.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\n**Step 1-1. Macro Variables**\n| Variable | Level | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| UST 10Y | 4.71%, up 0.44pts YoY | [Actual] Trading Economics/FRED 2026-08-21 |\n| Fed funds target | 3.50%\u20133.75%, held 9\u20133 vote | [Actual] FOMC 2026-07-29 |\n| DXY | ~98.6, down ~0.9% on 8/19 | [Actual] Trading Economics 2026-08-20 |\n| FOMC projected path | End-2026 3.8%, 2027 3.6%, 2028 3.4% | [Estimate] FundedFast/FRED median dots |\n| CPI / inflation | Not retrieved | [Unconfirmed] |\n| Credit spreads | Not retrieved | [Unconfirmed] |\n\n**Step 1-2. Regime Probability Distribution**\n| Regime | Probability | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reflation (high rates + growth) | 40% | 10Y at 4.7%, defense/industrial growth resilient |\n| Goldilocks (low rates + growth) | 25% | Fed pivoting to cuts in 2027\u201328 |\n| Stagflation (high rates + low growth) | 20% | Elevated rates with geopolitical supply risk |\n| Recession (low rates + low growth) | 15% | Cycle late-stage risk; defense is counter-cyclical |\n\n**Step 1-3. Sensitivity Axes (-3 to +3)**\n- Interest rate sensitivity: **-1** (long-duration EPS but low leverage)\n- Dollar sensitivity: **-2** (weak dollar supports international defense/commercial; some imported-cost risk)\n- Liquidity sensitivity: **-1** (equity-linked buyback but no balance-sheet dependence)\n- Economic cycle sensitivity: **-1** (defense counter-cyclical; commercial partial offset)\n- Commodity sensitivity: **0**\n\n**Step 1-4. Macro Alignment: Headwind (-0.5 conviction)**\n- 10Y at 4.71% pressures the 40x+ multiple; DXY weakness is a modest tailwind; defense budget